# The answer mode as a standing preference of the whole application (owner, 2026-11-21): a w.preferences key with its
# declared default. The chat's Fast | Thinking toggle states it, and so does a message that says one of the declared
# phrases below; what each mode allows a turn to try is declared in interpretation-policy.sop (app.interpret.mode).
# The stated value is a w.preferences.preference instance fact (source stated, scope app, at = one more than the latest),
# held in the session beside the areas; the latest stated value is in force, otherwise the default.
@pref.interaction.use core.use world=w.preferences prefix=false
@pref.interaction.mode w.preferences.default key=interaction.mode field=value value=fast scope=app about="the first acceptable answer"

# The words that state a value of a preference key. A message that contains one of them (as whole words) states that
# value; the rest of the message, if any, is read as a request as usual.
@pref.say.type core.type of=app.pref.say closed=true
@pref.say.key core.slot of=app.pref.say key=key kind=atom present=true
@pref.say.value core.slot of=app.pref.say key=value kind=atom present=true
@pref.say.text core.slot of=app.pref.say key=text kind=string many=true present=true
@pref.say.reply core.slot of=app.pref.say key=reply kind=string present=true
@pref.interaction.say.thinking app.pref.say key=interaction.mode value=thinking text="think harder" text="think carefully" text="think it through" text="take your time" text="take more time" text="be thorough" text="thinking mode" text="switch to thinking" reply="Thinking mode: I will try the alternatives before I answer."
@pref.interaction.say.fast app.pref.say key=interaction.mode value=fast text="be quick" text="be fast" text="quickly please" text="hurry up" text="fast mode" text="switch to fast" text="no need to think" text="answer quickly" reply="Fast mode: I will take the first reading that works."
